WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.940
When an old sin accuses you,

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.700
who has the final word?

3
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.460
Romans eight asks who can bring

4
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:11.800
a charge against those God has justified.

5
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.240
Paul points to Jesus Christ:

6
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:15.420
he died,

7
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:16.700
and he was raised.

8
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.680
He is at God’s right hand interceding

9
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:20.460
for his people.

10
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.260
The one who gave his life

11
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.040
for you is also the one who

12
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.080
speaks for you.

13
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.080
Your assurance rests on this living Savior.

14
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.860
An accusing memory cannot overturn God’s verdict

15
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:32.860
for those in Christ.

16
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:34.600
When guilt returns,

17
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.420
read these words slowly.

18
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.240
Bring your actual sin into the light,

19
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.380
and remember who stands for you.

20
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.780
You are held by the Savior who

21
00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:44.440
knows you.
